        "A simple offer could include:\n- A defined number of enhanced photographs.\n- One walkthrough video.\n- A specified number of revisions.\n- Delivery in agreed file formats.\n- A clear turnaround time.\nA retainer might cover a monthly volume of listings, but only offer it when the client has a recurring need.\nCosts and constraints\n- Image and video generation credits.\n- Time spent correcting outputs.\n- Client revisions.\n- Rights and permissions.\n- File storage and delivery.\n- The time required to manage multiple listings.\nThe source places this model in its B tier because it is relatively accessible and potentially high-margin at the tool-credit level, but it remains a service business: fulfilment time grows as the number of projects grows.\n2.6 First-client checklist\n- [ ] Identify a suitable agent, owner, or property manager.\n- [ ] Confirm permission to use the images.\n- [ ] Produce a small, accurate before-and-after sample.\n- [ ] Prepare one separate walkthrough example.\n- [ ] Check that the images do not misrepresent the property.\n- [ ] Send a concise, personalised offer.\n- [ ] Define deliverables, price, revisions, and rights in writing."
