        "AI website builders can make it faster to create a first draft. The service provider's job is to turn that draft into a useful business website with accurate information and clear paths to contact or book.",
        "The source stresses an important distinction: a website should not merely look attractive. It should help customers take action.\n5.1 Find businesses with visible website problems\nThe source demonstrates searching Google Maps for a local category—in the example, gardeners in Kent—and reviewing the websites linked from business listings.",
        "Other possible categories include local trades, service providers, and appointment-based businesses.",
        "Look for:\n- Outdated design.\n- Poor mobile layout.\n- Unclear service descriptions.\n- Missing or hard-to-find contact details.\n- Confusing navigation.\n- Broken links or forms.\n- Inconsistent opening hours or business information.\nDo not assume that an old-looking website is necessarily failing commercially. Treat it as a potential improvement opportunity and ask the owner about their goals.\n5.2 Gather accurate business information\nBefore building, review the business's available information:\n- Services offered.\n- Service areas.\n- Opening hours.\n- Contact details.\n- Existing customer reviews.\n- Brand name and identity.\n- Relevant images.\n- Booking or enquiry process.\nUse information the business has authorised you to use. Do not copy testimonials or images without appropriate permission.\n5.3 Generate a first website draft\nThe source demonstrates describing the business to an AI website builder.",
