        "The source's demonstration uses an AI builder to generate layout, text, and images, then adjusts the result manually or through further instructions.\n5.4 Review the generated website\nAI-generated websites are drafts, not finished deliverables.",
        "Check:\nBusiness accuracy\n- Correct business name and contact details.\n- Correct service list.\n- Correct location and service area.\n- Correct opening hours.\n- No invented claims, certifications, awards, or testimonials.\nUsability\n- Navigation works.\n- Contact buttons work.\n- Forms submit correctly.\n- Phone links use the correct number.\n- Important information is easy to find.\nMobile experience\n- Text is readable.\n- Buttons are easy to tap.\n- Images fit the screen.\n- Layout does not overflow.\n- Menus and forms work.\nTrust and presentation\n- Images are relevant and properly licensed.\n- Branding is consistent.\n- Copy is clear and specific.\n- No placeholder text remains.\n- The design does not make unsupported promises.\nTechnical checks\n- Links work.\n- Pages load.\n- Forms deliver enquiries to the right destination.\n- Domain and hosting arrangements are clear.\n- The client has access to the accounts and assets they own.\n5.5 Send a preview as a sample\nThe source recommends building a sample redesign and emailing the business:\n“Hi, I noticed your website wasn't working well on mobile, so I put together a quick redesign. Here's what it could look like. Happy to make changes.”",
