        "I put together a concept preview to show one possible direction. It is only a draft, and I would want your approval before using any content or publishing anything.",
        "Would you like me to send it over?\nAI advertising creative\nSubject: A creative concept for [Brand]",
        "Hi [Name],",
        "I have been exploring ways to produce product-focused ad concepts more efficiently. I prepared a sample concept using [approved or publicly supplied product information] to demonstrate the format.",
        "If this direction fits your brand, I would be happy to discuss a small paid test with agreed claims, creative scope, and usage rights.\nCustomer support assistant\nSubject: An idea for reducing repetitive support questions",
        "Hi [Name],",
        "I noticed your customers may have recurring questions about [relevant topic]. A support assistant could potentially handle straightforward questions using your approved policies and hand off anything uncertain to your team.",
        "I can show you a small demonstration using information you approve, then test it against common questions before anything goes live.",
        "Would that be useful?",
        "These are adaptable examples, not scripts that should be sent unchanged to every prospect.\n9.6 Follow up professionally\nIf a prospect does not reply, one concise follow-up may be appropriate. Do not repeatedly message people who have not shown interest or who ask you to stop.",
        "Keep a simple record of:\n- Business name.\n- Contact person.\n- Service offered.\n- Reason for contacting.\n- Date of first message.\n- Follow-up date.\n- Response.\n- Next step.\n- Permission or consent status where relevant."
